 "text": "9/29/26, 9:47 AM\nMeter reading results and period consumption are displayed per register.\n\nFrom the overview display, you can double-click on the net amounts to branch to the display of individual billing documents (for\nthe period billings or the period-end billing).\n\nYou can also simulate invoicing for the entire backbilling and/or period-end billing period using the results of the billing simulation.\nTo do so, you must first save (upload) the results of the billing simulation.\n\nFrom the overview of the simulation results, you can execute other simulation runs for the contract. This enables you to change the\nperiod consumption per billing period (for the period billings). In this way, the system can generate several simulated versions\nwhose results you can then compare.\n\nDynamic Period Control (DPC)\n\nUse\n\nWith dynamic period control (DPC), you can manage correction periods and periodic billing periods. You can generate billing\ndocuments that are based on estimated meter readings. You can use the meter reading functions to estimate the meter reading\n\nresults and save them to the database, or you can generate them during billing.\n\nEntering an actual meter reading result at any point triggers dynamic backbilling back to the last actual meter reading result. The\nsystem corrects all billing periods that are based on the estimated meter reading results.\n\nThe principle is explained in the following figure:\n\nDynamic Period Control\n\na\nMIRo                                                      MR1\n\nBilling based on actual meter readingresults\nInvoicing of billing documents\n\nee a a a\n\nMRo = 123                                                    MR:\n\n* Monthly billing based on actual meter readings - Start\n* Monthiyinvoicing of billing documents - Start\n\n[a\n\nMIRo 123        120         118         133        112           NMIR1\n\n* Monthly billing based on estimated meter readingresults\n* Monthly invoicing of billing documents\n\nFE\n\nname. 193         190          119          qa         4119        117 ==\n\n",
